    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The Japanese term '事業' (jigyō) primarily refers to 'business,' 'enterprise,' or 'project/undertaking,' which are specific, often large-scale or commercial, types of activities. It is much narrower than the general English 'activity,' which can encompass any action, pastime, or state of being active (e.g., leisure activities, daily activities, physical activity). It would not be natural for a general learner to use '事業' for the broad concept of 'activity.'",
